    <string name="battery_title">Keep Wisp awake</string>
    <string name="battery_message">Android puts apps to sleep to save power. Without an exemption, Wisp can miss calls when your screen has been off for a while.</string>
    <string name="fsi_title">Full-screen calls</string>
    <string name="fsi_message">Android 14 needs a separate permission before an incoming call can take over the screen. Without it, calls arrive as a banner at the top instead.</string>
    <string name="oem_title">One more setting</string>
    <string name="oem_samsung">Samsung phones put unused apps to sleep, which closes Wisp\'s connection. In Device care → Battery → Background usage limits, make sure Wisp is not in \"Sleeping apps\" or \"Deep sleeping apps\".</string>
    <string name="oem_huawei">Huawei phones close background apps aggressively. In Phone Manager → App launch, switch Wisp to manual and enable auto-launch, secondary launch and run in background.</string>
    <string name="oem_xiaomi">MIUI blocks background apps by default. In Security → Permissions → Autostart, turn Wisp on, and set its battery saver to \"No restrictions\".</string>
